# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Secrets and local configuration
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The MiniMax API key.  It is *never* needed for the default (GLM-only) run;
# it exists because the second provider was wired in and may be used again.
# It is read by the recording proxy, which injects it on the way out, so the
# key never reaches a job file or a trial log.
MINIMAX_KEY.txt
.env
*.key
*.pem

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Python environments and caches
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.venv/
.venv310/
.venv312/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The generated data
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# ``.cache/`` holds the two build artefacts that are large and are rebuilt by
# ``make``:
#
#   .cache/rsi-local/        the mini-swe-agent bundle that is bind-mounted
#                            into every trial container  (668 MB)
#   .cache/clawgym/          the HuggingFace dataset cache      (387 MB)
#
# ``work/`` holds everything a run or a build produces on the task side:
#
#   work/registry/          the OpenThoughts task registry   (23,225 tasks)
#   work/registry_clawgym/  the ClawGym task registry         (15,402 tasks)
#   work/tasks/             the instructions cut out of the published rollouts
#   work/pilot/             the pilot capture the wire checks read
#   work/dataset/           the merged datasets
#
# All of it is **rebuilt from public HuggingFace datasets** by
# ``make registry``, so it is not in git: 1.3 GB of task directories that
# anybody can regenerate in minutes.
/.cache/
/work/

# The converted dataset of each half, next to the harness that produced it.
/opencode_sft/dataset/
/mini_sft/dataset/

# The run outputs.
/runs/
/ledger/
/datasets/registry/
*.jsonl.gz

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The retired research line
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The RSI framework (a typed-configuration search over agent harnesses) is a
# separate research line and is **not** part of this repository.  These paths
# are ignored so that a working copy that still has them does not put them
# back into git by accident.
#
# Every pattern here is **anchored to the repository root** with a leading
# slash.  A bare ``tools/`` would match ``common/tools/`` at any depth, and
# git would then refuse to add a new file there.
/rsi/optimizer/
/rsi/evaluation/
/rsi/ledger/
/rsi/cli.py
/rsi/schema.py
/rsi/fields.py
/rsi/adapter.py
/rsi/benchmarks.py
/rsi/hop_runner.py
/rsi/rhi_agent.py
/rsi/ifeval_checkers.py
/harness/
/subsets/
/tests/
/synthetic-backup/
/tools/
/harbor/
/datasets/ifeval/
/datasets/base/tc/
/datasets/base/tb/
/scripts/build_ifeval_tasks.py
/scripts/calibrate.py
/scripts/make_real_splits.py
/scripts/patch_ineqmath_judge.py
/scripts/prepare_registry_tasks.py
/scripts/run_study.py
/scripts/separate_transfer_results.py
